[{"id":4890763266,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI4MgAg","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit_id":"c3cd2178f63f0a4e4b85ae4d91afe78eb4f27d01","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?u=9b90963f1b4f17720e50bbbe495fbe8c84c8bc8e&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","login":"TokageItLab","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab"},"body":"`current_bone < 0 || root_bone < 0` means that bones are not set. Therefore, I judge that checking if the bone index exceeds the size here is not the right place.\n\nThe correct way to fix would be to initialize the bone specification when a non-existent bone is found within `SkeletonModifier3D::_validate_bone_names()` and set its index to `-1`. This should prevent moving to subsequent lines due to the `current_bone < 0 || root_bone < 0` check.\n\nBTW, I think this issue exists in other places besides SpringBoneSimulator3D as well, so it would be ideal if consistent handling could be applied to all of them.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122053#pullrequestreview-4890763266","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122053","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-08-09T07:19:57Z"},{"id":4890917948,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI4V8PA","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit_id":"eb68661e11ce2c64d4c0544b24432cf663a1bcbe","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?u=9b90963f1b4f17720e50bbbe495fbe8c84c8bc8e&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4